    "notes": "The 511 m crossing has twelve curved radial gate leaves, tapered piers, a continuous cross-braced maintenance walk, a separately framed deck, individual chutes and a common apron. Two lower recesses interrupt the solid right wing. The separate right-bank powerhouse follows its mapped plan. The viewer renders the reservoir at the representative 269.75 m full-pool stage and the Krishna tailwater at 190 m. The twelve gate bays, chute, lip and the right-bank powerhouse remain visible. The authored crest deck replaces both mapped bridge fragments and joins the native approaches at 275.54 m. The tailwater, local bank grades and powerhouse platform are representative exterior estimates. Some outer shoreline edges remain sharp in the coarse terrain. The model depicts static gates and covers the right-bank plant exterior. The host supplies the matching Protomaps feature IDs and terrain samples fine enough to resolve the graded shoulders."
  },
